TY  - CONF
TI  - A Hybrid LSTM-GARCH Model Integrating Volatility Factors from the US Financial Markets
AU  - Zhang, Xiaoliang
AB  - This paper proposes a hybrid LSTM-GARCH model that integrates volatility factors from the US financial market, positioning the GARCH component as the core to enhance the robustness of the prediction system under uncertain environments. To optimize the effectiveness of input features, based on the principles of correlation, significance, and quantifiability, a method combining mutual information entropy and variance contribution is used to select five core volatility factors: Dow Jones Industrial Average return, US dollar index volatility, US 10-year Treasury yield, WTI crude oil futures price volatility, and S&P 500 volatility index (VIX), which are then standardized and preprocessed. The model adopts a hierarchical sequential architecture of "factor input layer → LSTM time series feature extraction layer → feature fusion layer → GARCH robustness enhancement layer → volatility output layer,"constructing an original fitting formula to integrate the time series features extracted by LSTM into the GARCH model, achieving a complementary balance between prediction accuracy and robustness. Using daily data from the US financial market from 2018 to 2024 as experimental samples, multiple comparative experiments were conducted using single LSTM, single GARCH (1,1), traditional ARIMA (2,1,1), and a hybrid LSTM-GRU model as benchmark models. The results show that the proposed model significantly outperforms all benchmark models in terms of accuracy, with a MAE of 0.0213±0.0012, RMSE of 0.0307±0.0018, and MAPE of 1.89%±0.12%, representing a reduction of 23.1%-42.7% in MAPE compared to different benchmark models. In terms of robustness, the error fluctuation coefficient is only 0.0042 under extreme market conditions, and the MAPE change rate is 8.7% at a noise level of 0.2, demonstrating excellent predictive stability and providing an effective technical solution for financial risk modeling and volatility prediction. © 2026 Copyright held by the owner/author(s).
