TI  - Multi-step-ahead Crude Oil Price Forecasting Based on Autoregressive Integrated Moving Average and Improved Particle Swarm Optimization-enhanced Gated Recurrent Unit
AU  - Jiao, Xingrui
AU  - Jia, Susan
AB  - Crude oil price volatility has a strong influence on the stability of the global energy market. Therefore, both traders and policy makers have been interested in the accurate forecast of crude oil price so as to prevent large losses and to stabilize the market. This study forecasts crude oil price based on autoregressive integrated moving average ARIMA and improved particle swarm optimization (IPSO)-enhanced gated recurrent unit (GRU) with the daily data of West Texas Intermediate (WTI) crude oil spot prices covering a period of 714 days. Results suggest that GRU consistently enhances ARIMA by addressing the non-linear portion of the time series, but IPSO-enhanced GRU has always achieved the best performance. For twenty-step forecasting, the overall reduction of RMSE is as much as 53%, which significantly raises the prediction accuracy.
