TI  - Enhanced Crude Oil Price Forecasting with CEEMDAN-ARIMA Hybrid Model
AU  - Pal, Raman Kumar
AU  - Padhan, Chinmaya Ranjan
AU  - Panigrahi, Sibarama
AB  - Fluctuations in crude oil prices (COP) have a very significant impact on global economies, energy policies, and financial markets. It is critical for stakeholders (policymakers, investors, and industries) to accurately predict COP to reduce risk and improve decision making. In order to identify important patterns and trends, this study breaks down daily, weekly, and monthly COP data into intrinsic mode functions (IMFs) using the Complete Ensemble Empirical Mode Decomposition with Adaptive Noise (CEEMDAN) approach. The decomposed components are examined using a variety of deep learning, machine learning, and statistical techniques, including linear regression, ridge regression, ElasticNet, Huber regression, and random forest, as well as neural networks such as long short-term memory (LSTM), gated recurrent unit (GRU), and statistical models such as auto-regressive integrated moving average (ARIMA), generalized autoregressive conditional heteroskedasticity (GARCH). Model performance is evaluated using different deterministic accuracy metrics. Among the models tested, the CEEMDANARIMA demonstrates superior accuracy and robustness across all evaluation criteria. The findings underscore the effectiveness of CEEMDAN-based decomposition combined with ARIMA for precise prediction of COP, providing valuable insights for strategic decision making in energy markets.
