TI  - Wavelet-Enhanced Blending Ensemble of CNN, LSTM, and GRU for Crude Oil Futures Price Prediction
AU  - Nandeshwar, Tushar Babulal
AU  - Sharma, Akanksha
AU  - Gupta, Abhinav
AU  - Verma, Chandan Kumar
AB  - Crude oil futures price prediction is an essential tool for risk management, energy planning, and financial market analysis. The volatile, non-linear nature of crude oil prices poses significant challenges for traditional models, which often fail to capture the complex temporal dependencies and noise inherent in commodity markets. This research proposes a robust ensemble framework to improve the precision and stability of crude oil price prediction. This approach integrates three distinct architectures-CNN, LSTM, and GRU-using a blending strategy with a linear regression-based meta-learner. To improve signal quality and model efficiency, the discrete wavelet transform (DWT) is employed for denoising, and Pearson correlation coefficient is used to select the most informative technical indicators. Model performance is evaluated using RMSE, MAE, R<sup>2</sup> score, Max Error, and Directional Accuracy Ratio (DAR). Experimental results show the ensemble consistently outperforms individual models across all metrics. Statistical validation using the DieboldMariano test confirms the ensemble's superiority. The framework improves predictive accuracy while enhancing robustness and generalization, offering a scalable solution for real-world financial forecasting.
