TI  - Ensemble Deep Learning for Small-Sample Time Series Forecasting
AU  - Li, Kunjian
AU  - Chen, Qichun
AB  - This paper investigates the efficacy of ensemble deep learning architectures for time series forecasting in small-sample settings, with a focus on regional energy markets. Traditional forecasting methods often falter in scenarios with limited data availability and high volatility, underscoring the need for more robust and adaptive approaches. We propose and benchmark a series of hybrid models across multiple performance metrics. Our empirical analysis, using daily trading records from two regional emissions exchanges as a proxy for energy market behavior, demonstrates that attention-enhanced and residual-learning-based ensembles significantly outperform baseline models in both accuracy and directional reliability. These findings highlight the potential of ensemble architectures to improve prediction robustness in low-data, high-uncertainty forecasting environments.
