AU  - Chen, Xingying
AU  - Shao, Jia
AU  - Zheng, Jin
AU  - Wang, Bo
AU  - Gan, Lei
AU  - Yu, Kun
AB  - Spot market electricity price fluctuations can expose market participants to substantial financial risks if not accurately forecasted. Traditional statistical models (e.g., ARIMA) can capture linear trends but struggle with complex nonlinear relationships, while pure neural network models (e.g., Transformer) are insufficiently sensitive to random fluctuations. To address both persistent price trends and transient volatility, this paper combines Transformer with stochastic differential equations driven by Ornstein-Uhlenbeck process. Compared to ARIMA, the proposed model achieves an average MAE reduction of approximately 45 %, along with comparable improvements in RMSE and MAPE and a significant boost in \mathbfR^\mathbf2. Against a standalone Transformer, it also exhibits substantial performance gains across all key metrics.
