TI  - A Hybrid PLO-Transformer-CEEMDAN Model for Natural Gas Price Forecasting
AU  - Wang, Xiang
AU  - Wang, Hao
AU  - Wang, Zirong
AU  - Wu, Di
AU  - Xue, Yuan
AU  - Ye, Lingxiao
AU  - Zhang, Yucong
T2  - IEEE Access
AB  - To address the nonlinear and non-stationary characteristics of natural gas prices, this study proposes a hybrid PLO-Transformer-CEEMDAN forecasting framework. The model integrates weight optimization, multi-scale trend extraction, and residual correction, effectively utilizing 27 heterogeneous features—including Google Trends indicators—to improve predictive accuracy. Empirical evaluations on Henry Hub monthly data (2004–2024) show that the model achieves exceptional forecasting performance (RMSE: 0.0257, R2: 0.9998), representing a 92.87% RMSE reduction compared to the baseline Transformer. Notably, incorporating Google Trends alone leads to a 30.91% improvement in accuracy, underscoring its value in capturing market sentiment prior to price changes. Overall, the proposed method significantly outperforms conventional benchmarks in both predictive precision and generalization ability, offering a robust tool for energy price forecasting and market risk assessment.
