TY  - CONF
TI  - A Hybrid Recommender System for Predicting Gold Prices Using Financial and Temporal Data
AU  - Bhaskaran, S.
AU  - N, Venkata Subramanian
AB  - Predicting the cost of gold is essential in financial decision-making and investment planning. The traditional models are generated by the majority of econometric or time-series methods, but they do not address the specifics of investment behavior of users. In the study we develop a hybrid recommender system based on collaborative filtering, content-based analysis and temporal modeling to predict the price of gold and recommend investment activities. We make use of data on gold prices as well as pertinent data on the macroeconomy and preference data of simulated investors to make up a complete predictive model. Findings indicate that the combination of various techniques is more accurate than individual methods. The resulting model is full of customized information and offers better forecasting abilities. This research shows the possibility of the recommended systems not bound to e-commerce as in the finance and commodity sectors.
