TI  - Predictive Accuracy Comparison Between Machine Learning and Deep Learning Frameworks in Energy Stock Forecasting
AU  - K, Krishna Kumar.
AU  - Aalam, S. Shiek
AU  - Sonya, A.
AU  - K, Divya.
AU  - S, Sakthivel.
AU  - S, Yuvaraj.
AB  - The unpredictability of financial markets, driven by their volatility and nonlinear patterns, makes accurate stock price forecasting a difficult task. This study investigates the predictive capability of Machine Learning(ML) and Deep Learning(DL) models by comparing the performance of LSTM networks with XGBoost regression for forecasting Indian energy sector stocks. One year of historical stock price data was retrieved from the Yahoo Finance platform, which served as the primary data source for this study, and technical indicators such as exponential moving averages (EMA-5, EMA-10) were incorporated as features. Training and validation were performed on stock data from several petroleum and oil sector companies, and predictive accuracy was measured using MAE, RMSE, and R2 metrics. Results show that XGBoost outperformed LSTM, achieving a lower average RMSE (4.96 vs. 7.14) and higher average R2 (0.9949 vs. 0.9857), indicating superior error minimization and generalization. The results emphasize the strength of ensemble-based approaches such as XGBoost in modeling intricate stock market behaviors, demonstrating their reliability for short-term forecasting when compared to deep learning models.
