TI  - BSTFN: A Bayesian Spatio-Temporal Fusion Network for Electric Power Data Asset Circulation Prediction
AU  - Meng, Zhipeng
AU  - Meng, Qi
AU  - Liu, Kaijie
AU  - Chen, Zhaoli
AU  - Feng, Songyao
AB  - The power system, as a critical part of national infrastructure, faces many challenges, such as energy demand fluctuations, equipment aging, and market volatility, making accurate prediction of power data asset flow difficult. Traditional forecasting methods, while effective in certain conditions, often fail to meet the high accuracy and robustness required in complex power system scenarios. To address these challenges, this paper proposes the Bayesian Spatio-Temporal Fusion Network (BSTFN), which integrates Bayesian inference, dynamic graph neural networks (GNN), and a spatio-temporal interaction attention mechanism to tackle the uncertainty and complex spatio-temporal dependencies in power data asset flow prediction. BSTFN utilizes Bayesian inference to handle uncertainty and dynamic GNNs to capture the evolving relationships within the power system. Additionally, the spatio-temporal interaction attention mechanism enhances the model's ability to capture spatio-temporal dependencies. Ablation experiments have been conducted to validate the importance of each module. The experimental results demonstrate that BSTFN outperforms existing comparative models on the PJM and UCI datasets, exhibiting higher accuracy and robustness. The model effectively enhances prediction performance and showcases its potential application in complex power data scenarios.
