TI  - Comparison of Regression and Classification Models for Forecasting Thai Gold Prices
AU  - Htet, Thinzar
AU  - Kurubanjerdjit, Nilubon
AU  - Nupap, Soontarin
AU  - Htay, Tint Tint
AB  - Accurate forecasting of gold prices is essential for investors, policymakers, and businesses due to gold's role as a financial asset and market hedge. This study compares classification and regression models to predict Thai domestic gold prices using daily price data and macroeconomic indicators. Classification models were applied to forecast short-term trends ("Up," "Down," "Neutral"), while regression models predicted the actual price. A time-series cross-validation approach with lagged and rolling features captured temporal dependencies in the data. Results indicate that Ridge Regression (alpha=1) achieved the lowest mean absolute error and highest R2, demonstrating superior predictive performance for daily prices, while Logistic Regression achieved the highest F1-score for trend prediction. The findings highlight the effectiveness of regularised regression in modelling gold price dynamics and the challenges of trend classification due to market volatility and class imbalance.
