TI  - Optimizing FAANG Stock Forecasting: The Power of Feature Engineering and LSTM in Financial Analysis
AU  - Tiwari, Priyanshu
AU  - Patil, Soumya
AU  - Ambareesh, S
AU  - Raj, Rishabh
AB  - The unprecedented growth and market capitalization of the FAANG stocks - Facebook, Amazon, Apple, Netflix, and Google (Alphabet) - have mushroomed into the pay-off race of the leaders of the global financial market. Stock price volatility prediction attracts the focus of the investors and analysts in the pursuit of profit maximization relying on market movements. In order to enhance the precision of stock price predictions for FAANG companies, other more intricate methods for feature engineering are also coupled together with LSTM neural networks. Stock price dynamic intricacies are being reflected by the model using the complete set of financial indicators, predictive analytics, and market sentiment data as features. The work showed a phenomenal application of LSTM networks in the analysis and prediction of stock price trends compared to the classic methods on the sequential-by-nature front dealing with long dependencies. It is actually possible to build a strong base of data enabling the detection of such elusive trends in the performances of FAANG stocks and technical indicators, sentiment analysis, or economic metrics, for instance, thereby getting into working order for LSTM modeling. Results from experiments show the method provides better accuracy and reliability than conventional machine learning models, thus collecting valuable insights for certain financial-forecasting purposes. The paper serves as a demonstration illustrates how feature engineering and LSTM might be combined to improve predicting financial markets and provides one solution for investors, financial analysts, and policymakers who look to make informed investment decisions.
