TI  - Probabilistic Forecasting of Day-Ahead Electricity Prices in Germany: A Hybrid Deep Learning and Mixture Distribution Approach
AU  - Wang, Zhikun
AU  - Hua, Haochen
AU  - Zhou, Yang
AU  - Zheng, Jin
AB  - The increasing integration of renewable energy has introduced severe volatility to day-ahead electricity markets, characterized by zero-price agglomerations and highly asymmetric tail risks. Traditional models struggle to capture these complex dynamics. This paper proposes a novel two-stage hybrid probabilistic forecasting framework. First, an Informer neural network efficiently extracts long-range deterministic trends. Second, the forecasting residuals are modeled using a conditional zero-inflated skewed-t distribution. The distribution’s shape parameters are explicitly mapped to fundamental physical drivers via generalized linear models (GLM) and calibrated by minimizing the continuous ranked probability score (CRPS). Evaluated on the highly volatile German1|5-minute market, the proposed framework exhibits profound physical interpretability and exceptional probabilistic calibration. It effectively hedges against deep negative prices and dynamically adjusts prediction intervals to envelop extreme spikes, providing a robust risk management tool.
