TI  - Research on Optimization of Enterprise Electricity Consumption Strategy and Cost Control Based on Electricity Price Signal
AU  - Xiang, Yang
AU  - Chong, Lei
AB  - Against the backdrop of the deepening reform of the energy market, which has triggered sharp fluctuations in electricity prices, the electricity costs of large electricityconsuming enterprises have surged dramatically, and traditional electricity consumption models struggle to adapt to the dynamic electricity price environment. To address this issue, this paper proposes an integrated optimization model featuring “data-driven -predictive modeling-strategy optimization-collaborative regulation”: by analyzing enterprises' electricity consumption characteristics and leveraging high-precision models to accurately predict future electricity loads and prices, it establishes a dynamic electricity price classification and load priority mechanism, and further integrates demand response and energy storage systems to form a comprehensive electricity optimization solution. Taking energy conservation and emission reduction as the means to regulate electricity consumption strategies, this model not only reduces enterprises' electricity costs but also contributes to the achievement of the “dual carbon” goals; comparative experiments have verified its favorable application effects.
