TI  - A Learning based Bidding Strategy for Energy Arbitrage of Battery Energy Storage Systems in Day-Ahead Electricity Market
AU  - Sun, Hanxi
AU  - Xu, Yan
AU  - Xia, Yang
AU  - Xie, Dunjian
AU  - Zhang, Rui
AB  - Bidding under uncertain electricity prices remains a challenge for battery energy storage systems (BESS). This paper proposes a deep reinforcement learning based bidding strategy for battery energy storage systems to arbitrage in day-ahead electricity markets. First of all, a data-driven decision-making framework is designed to maximize the BESS's profit from market participation, which only relies on historical price data without the need for additional forecasting modules. Secondly, a confidence function is developed to evaluate the confidence of the bidding decision, enabling smoother and more adaptive bidding decisions for BESS under market uncertainties. During training, a Long Short-Term Memory (LSTM) network is enhanced with Proximal Policy Optimization (PPO) to capture temporal price features, which further improves decision-making. Case studies using three years of Australian market data demonstrate that the proposed method achieves stable convergence, high arbitrage revenue, and safe SoC compliance.
