TI  - Optimization of Multi-Market Transaction Decisions for Data-Driven Electric Vehicle Aggregators
AU  - Wang, Wen
AU  - Yang, Ye
AU  - Fang, Xiangliang
AU  - Zhang, Xiaoqing
AU  - Li, Yao
AU  - Li, Min
AU  - Liu, Sihua
AU  - Li, Peijun
AB  - As the “dual carbon” strategy progresses and the penetration rate of new energy continues to rise, electric vehicles (EVs) are increasingly playing a prominent role in power systems as flexible, adjustable load resources. Aggregators, by consolidating a large number of EV resources, have the potential to participate in diverse power markets such as the electricity energy market, ancillary services market, and demand response market. However, due to factors such as electricity price fluctuations, uncertainty in user charging behavior, and differences in market mechanisms, aggregators face complex and dynamic challenges in their trading decisions. This paper addresses the multi-market transaction challenges faced by EV aggregators by establishing a data-driven decision optimization framework. First, by introducing deep learning methods, the framework achieves high-precision predictions of electric vehicle user load behavior and electricity market prices. Second, a multiobjective robust optimization model is constructed to formulate cross-market participation strategies, considering factors such as revenue maximization, battery health, and user satisfaction. Finally, simulation verification is conducted in multiple typical urban distribution network scenarios to assess the robustness and economic viability of the strategies under different uncertainty conditions.
