TI  - Investigating and Constructing an Advanced Nonlinear Deep Learning Model for Crude Oil Price Prediction
AU  - Shiva, J
AU  - Reddy, A Srinish
AU  - Devadasu, G
AU  - Gulzar, M D
AU  - P.Ramya
AU  - K.Rohini
AB  - Investigating and Building an Advanced Nonlinear Deep Learning Model for Crude Oil Price Prediction Introduction: Many economic, geopolitical, and commercial factors make predicting crude oil prices a difficult nonlinear process. Dealing with the intricate network patterns generated during oil price fluctuations, conventional econometrics mixed with statistical modeling techniques frequently fall short. This paper assesses the evolution of an improved nonlinear deep learning system meant to predict crude oil prices. By means of RNNs and LSTM networks, transformer-based systems allow computers to predict prices by accuracy and dependability. Best prediction outcomes are produced by full data processing along with attribute generation and parameter adjustment. By means of a model that analyzes past price patterns relating to macroeconomic performance elements and financial news emotional data, it may perform more accurately for improved market understanding. Using MAE and RMSE performance measures, this model is compared to statistical techniques and conventional machine learning models. Experimental data indicates that over market volatility evaluations and price movement, deep learning models constructed with non-linear structures outperform conventional analysis methods. The study shows good uses of artificial intelligence for energy economics that will generate better data-based decision structures over the oil market.
