TI  - Quantum-Inspired Support Vector Regression with Deep Learning for Gold Price Forecasting
AU  - Kaur, Harinder
AU  - Kaur, Sarabjit
AU  - Sharma, Atipriya
AU  - Shelke, Nilesh
AB  - Gold price prediction plays important role for making financial decisions for investors, policymakers and economists. However a manual prediction of the gold prices is difficult due to its dependency on various economic factors. The traditional machine learning models are not able to find the complex relationships among data. To address this problem, this paper has proposed Quantum-Inspired Support Vector Regression (QI-SVR). This technique combines the SVT model quantum based optimization process. This quantum model is able to handle nonlinear patterns. The experiments are performed on dataset which includes factors like gold prices, the USD index, crude oil prices, silver prices, and the S&P index. The performance of proposed technique is compared with existing techniques such as ARIMS, LSTM and other hybrid models. The experimental results shows that the proposed QI-SVR is effective with R2 score of 0.971, RMSE of 22.34, and MAPE of 2.11%. Further, this study shows that quantum-inspired learning can be an effective and efficient way to forecast financial time series.
